      "text": "To determine the length of segment \\( BC \\) in the right triangles \\( ABC \\) and \\( ABD \\), we need to use the Pythagorean theorem. Let's start by analyzing the given information and setting up the necessary equations.\n\nFirst, consider triangle \\( ABD \\). Since \\( ABD \\) is a right triangle with \\( AD \\) perpendicular to \\( BD \\), we can label the lengths as follows:\n- \\( AD = 16 \\)\n- \\( BD = 19 \\)\n\nWe need to find the length of \\( AB \\). Using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABD \\):\n\\[\nAB^2 + AD^2 = BD^2\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\nAB^2 + 16^2 = 19^2\n\\]\n\\[\nAB^2 + 256 = 361\n\\]\n\\[\nAB^2 = 361 - 256\n\\]\n\\[\nAB^2 = 105\n\\]\n\\[\nAB = \\sqrt{105}\n\\]\n\nNext, consider triangle \\( ABC \\). Since \\( B \\) is at the top of the triangle and \\( BC \\) is a leg of the right triangle, we can label the lengths as follows:\n- \\( AB = \\sqrt{105} \\)\n- \\( AD = 16 \\)\n- \\( BC \\) is the leg of the right triangle \\( ABC \\)\n\nTo find \\( BC \\), we need to use the Pythagorean theorem again. Let \\( AC \\) be the hypotenuse of triangle \\( ABC \\). We know that \\( AC \\) is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with \\( AB \\) and \\( BD \\) as the legs. However, we need to find \\( BC \\) directly.\n\nSince \\( BD = 19 \\) and \\( AD = 16 \\), we can use the fact that \\( BC \\) is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with \\( AB \\) and \\( AD \\) as the legs. We need to find the length of \\( AC \\) first.\n\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABD \\) again:\n\\[\nAC^2 = AB^2 + AD^2\n\\]\n\\[\nAC^2 = (\\sqrt{105})^2 + 16^2\n\\]\n\\[\nAC^2 = 105 + 256\n\\]\n\\[\nAC^2 = 361\n\\]\n\\[\nAC = \\sqrt{361}\n\\]\n\\[\nAC = 19\n\\]\n\nNow, we use the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABC \\) with \\( AB \\) and \\( BC \\) as the legs:\n\\[\nAC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2\n\\]\n\\[\n19^2 = (\\sqrt{105})^2 + BC^2\n\\]\n\\[\n361 = 105 + BC^2\n\\]\n\\[\nBC^2 = 361 - 105\n\\]\n\\[\nBC^2 = 256\n\\]\n\\[\nBC = \\sqrt{256}\n\\]\n\\[\nBC = 16\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of segment \\( BC \\) is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
